  "case_reason": "The counterexample relies on an unsupported premise that a model trained on a narrow distribution (e.g., math word problems) inherently utilizes 'broad general knowledge' from pre-training to solve them. This assumes the reasoning chains required for such problems necessarily depend on external broad knowledge rather than specific, domain-relevant patterns learned within the narrow scope itself.",
